{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a79aae02405191df","name":"Predator-Class Starfighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-a79aae02405191df","title":"Predator-Class Starfighter","revision":18775,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:42:52Z","sha256":"bc0bbac722dea3c56748bca2cde4dd95a9066f12f4ce8c64dcd5bb1e5e03fe6f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18775","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Predator-Class%20Starfighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a79aae02405191df","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Fel Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Fel_Empire","referenceId":"reference:45bef1c82bffe9c1"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Knights","referenceId":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter is one of the foremost weapons in Darth Krayt's Imperial Fleet. Designed over a hundred years after the Empire's defeat at ",{"tag":"a","children":["Endor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Endor"},", the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter bears more than just a passing resemblance to the Imperial ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"},". However, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter is far more than just ",{"tag":"a","children":["Turbolaser"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Turbolaser","referenceId":"reference:3f6c338dc202fcde"}," fodder; these ships are fast, agile, shielded, and a far more formidable foe than even the most advanced ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," used during the Galactic Civil War. These ships boast ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrives"}," that allow them to travel over long distances without the need of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},", though most Imperial vessels carry a complement of ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighters for protection.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter has two variant cockpit styles; the more traditional, ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"},"-like cockpit is reserved for squad leaders and commanders, while the remaining ships have a cockpit with a diagonally slashed set of viewing slots. Though the standard cockpit offers a reduced view of the battlefield, the interior of a ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter contains advanced computer technology with sophisticated heads-up displays to compensate for the reduction in visibility.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The mainstay of the Imperial Navy's Starfighter Corps, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter from Sienar Fleet Systems answers the Empire's basic need for a space superiority fighter that, like the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebellion Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebellion_Era"},", can also be mass produced. Faster and more agile than past Sienar designs, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter boasts shielding to help protect it from those rare shots that manage to hit the fighter. Unlike its TIE predecessors, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter is fitted with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"},", making it suitable for long-distance strike missions.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["There are two primary cockpit styles among ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighters. The standard configuration has a somewhat reduced view of the battlefield, instead encouraging the pilot to rely on heads-up displays and computer-enhanced targeting and sensor data. Squadron leaders and wing commanders have a more traditional ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"},"-style cockpit, which allows for better visual scanning and situational assessment. ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighters are kept in racks aboard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," and can be launched with speed from those ships' hangars.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter shares many of the characteristics of the TIE-Series, most notably the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Defender"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Defender","referenceId":"reference:577e3c60924dbda0"},". Though more lightly armed, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter boasts shields and increased hull strength that makes a single ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class ship last longer in combat. The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter is also incredibly fast and agile, making it more adept at avoiding incoming attacks than its predecessors. In fact, the combination of enhanced durability with technology designed to avoid taking damage at all makes the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter a fearsome ship to face in combat.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter is primarily used as a space superiority fighter. Launched out of special hanging racks aboard larger ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},", a ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter does not need to swarm over it's enemies in huge numbers like it's predecessors. Instead, small wings or squadrons of ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighters are dispatched to handle most problems, with impressive results. A ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter can stand up to nearly any comparable ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},", including the ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-83 TwinTail Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-83_TwinTail_Starfighters?action=edit&redlink=1"},", and as such Darth Krayt's Empire has seen a much higher survival rate among pilots of ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class ships than the Empire ever did with ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"}," pilots. The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter is also the favored Starfighter of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Knights","referenceId":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559"},", whose Force-assisted piloting makes them as deadly in a cockpit as they are in a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," duel.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Predator"]},"-Class Starfighter Statistics (CL 11)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +10; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 21 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 24; +7 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 100; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 10; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"},": 15; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 44\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Fly 16 Squares (",{"tag":"a","chi